  "notes": "COMPOUND VERB:\n{駆|か}ける (to run, to gallop) + {抜|ぬ}ける (to pass through)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive) - takes を for the place being passed through\n\nFIGURATIVE USE:\nOften used poetically to describe wind, light, or time passing quickly through something.\n\nRELATED COMPOUND VERBS:\n- {走|はし}り{抜|ぬ}ける: to run through (similar meaning)\n- {駆|か}け{回|まわ}る: to run around\n- {突|つ}き{抜|ぬ}ける: to pierce through",
